title: An answer that is not JSON must not pass as a success
updated: 2026-10-20T09:29:24Z
---

An HTTP 200 with a body that is not JSON is treated as a success.

lib/WWW/PayPal/Role/HTTP.pm:191-197 decodes the body only when it starts with { or [. A body that starts with anything else (the HTML login page of a captive portal or a proxy, for example) leaves $data undef and $broken 0, so the error branch at :199 does not fire and the method returns undef without an error.

The failure surfaces much later and somewhere else: $pp->request(GET => ...) returns UNDEF, $pp->orders->get($id) returns an object, and the first access to a field dies with "Can't use an undefined value as a HASH reference at lib/WWW/PayPal/Order.pm line 52". The caller gets neither status nor path.

Decide: a body that is not empty and does not parse as JSON is raised as WWW::PayPal::Error with status, method and path. An empty body (204) stays allowed, otherwise notifications.webhooks.delete (lib/WWW/PayPal/API/Webhooks.pm:247) breaks.

The test that holds this down must be red against the old lib/ and fail as a failed expectation, not as a die.

2026-10-20 09:16 Done: every non-empty body is decoded in Role::HTTP::request; a body that is not a JSON object/array is thrown as WWW::PayPal::Error with status, method, path, body and data. A 2xx with a broken body says 'HTTP 200: the answer was no JSON', a status >= 300 keeps the status line or PayPal's message. An empty body (204) stays allowed. Commit 957a1b3.

2026-10-20 09:16 Decision beyond the letter of the card: a body that decodes to a scalar or to null ('123', 'null') is treated like a broken body, because request() must not hand a scalar or an undef to the controllers - the silent-undef class of bug the card is about would survive otherwise. PayPal answers with an object or an array, so nothing legitimate is affected.
